<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/cloud_cover_na/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>White = cloud tops (multi-satellite infrared, day + night); transparent = clear sky or no satellite coverage. Infrared brightness, not a cloud-cover percentage.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: GOES-19/18 ABI infrared + Himawari-9 infrared (via NASA GIBS) + Meteosat SEVIRI infrared imagery (via EUMETSAT EUMETView) + VIIRS daily polar supplement (via NASA GIBS)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of all other layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>☁️ LIVE CLOUD COVER — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/North_America_Live_Cloud_Cover.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>300</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
